# Multi-Agent Team Orchestration for Virtual Office

This project is configured with a specialized Virtual Office Multi-Agent Team defined in [`.agents/agents.json`](file:///Users/ahmadshahwaiz/Desktop/Virtual Office/.agents/agents.json).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### 🎯 ALWAYS INVOKE `android-pm` FIRST (PRIMARY ORCHESTRATOR)!
> **The 1st agent in the active roster (`android-pm`) is the Primary Orchestrator.**
> All other agents (`android-tech-lead`, `android-dev`, `android-tester`) operate as its specialized subagents.
> When a user request arrives (feature development, architecture, testing, or bug fixes):
> 1. **Do not begin executing tasks directly as a single monolithic agent.**
> 2. **Invoke `android-pm` (Android Product Lead) first** as the Primary Orchestrator using `invoke_subagent`.
> 3. **`android-pm`** breaks down the user request into structured sprint tasks with clear acceptance criteria following [`task-decomposition`](file:///Users/ahmadshahwaiz/Desktop/Virtual Office/.agents/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md), and delegates to its subagents according to the delegation graph below.

---

